<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish unemployment falls to 262,400 in Jan - CSO.</title>
<headline>Irish unemployment falls to 262,400 in Jan - CSO.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of those claiming unemployment benefit fell to a seasonally adjusted 262,400 in January from 266,000 in December, Central Statistics Office figures show.</p>
<p>			   Unadjusted	    Adjusted</p>
<p> Latest		  268,890		 262,400</p>
<p> Previous		270,156		 266,000</p>
<p> Year-ago		287,997		 281,500</p>
<p>(No percentages of the total workforce were given.) -- Dublin newsroom 353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
